# ADR-140-AMEND-1 — Cure discipline: cure the class, not the example

**Status:** ACCEPTED (lands only through the PLAN-189 W0 signed ceremony; the Owner's `.asc` on the W0 sentinel is the ratification)
**Date:** 2026-09-15 (proposed) / 2026-09-16 (accepted at signature)
**Enforcement commit:** n/a — doctrine clause in `PROTOCOL.md` §Cure discipline, checklist-enforced (the same enforcement model as ADR-140 §Receiving review and PROTOCOL.md §Honest limitation: no blocking hook). The mechanical companions are PLAN-189 W2 (rail telemetry) and W3 (record safeguard), each in its own signature.
**Decision drivers:** ceremonies of 6, 11, 12 and 27 rounds; the measured cause is the SHAPE of the cure, not the reviewer; three cheaper hypotheses refuted by data.

## §1 What this amendment changes

ADR-140 governs how review is **received** (read whole, restate, verify
against code, reasoned pushback, implement per item). It says nothing about
what a valid **cure** is. This amendment adds one clause to `PROTOCOL.md`,
§Cure discipline, immediately after §Receiving review:

- every finding carries a **class** named by the author of the cure in the
  round record (one `Class:` line per finding);
- the **second occurrence** of the same class in the same ceremony forbids a
  cure that is another example: either the surface is removed (architecture
  change) or the record carries a written impossibility plus a **named risk
  acceptance**;
- a record showing a second occurrence with neither is a **visible
  violation** of the clause — a blocking finding against the record itself.

"Same class" is decided by the author against either test: same property
violated, or same input surface (Owner decision 7, 2026-09-15). Nothing in
ADR-140 is weakened or removed; the receiving discipline stands unchanged.

## §2 Evidence — measured, sources on the record

All figures below are read from `.claude/plans/PLAN-189-cure-quality-and-rail-instrumentation.md` §Context and the S352 measurements it cites; none is new here.

1. **The cheap hypotheses died against data.** (a) "the rail produces noise" —
   refuted: thematic class of a finding is not a false-positive rate, and
   32.2 % of the census sat in "unclassified" (5.9 % or 38.1 % depending on
   reclassification). (b) "a mechanical ceiling of 3 rounds" — refuted by the
   corpus: validity does NOT decay with the round (r1-r3 93 %, r4-r7 93 %,
   r8+ 91 %; 178 marks REAL/VERIFIED against 13 REFUTED/PUSHBACK). A ceiling
   would cut mostly valid findings. (c) "stop when no new P0/P1" — refuted:
   "none NEW" lets an OLD blocker stay open, and a round without detection
   does not demonstrate absence.
2. **Cure by enumeration.** In the PLAN-179 ceremony, `_sanitize_memory_basename`
   was BYTE-IDENTICAL between the r6 and the r15 candidates: the "late" P1
   had existed since r6. Round r22 records itself as the FIFTH round of the
   same class (spaces, hyphens, concatenation, limits) and only then REMOVES
   the surface. Each earlier cure closed the cited example and left the
   class open; the reviewer found the next variant.
3. **Regression by cure.** The cure of the r9 P2 introduced `-m`; the r26 P1
   reports the union of the parents' diffs caused by that behaviour. The
   test created in r9 stayed GREEN — a covered example does not cover the
   class. (This is the evidence for PLAN-189 W1, which lands in its own
   signature; it is cited here because the two mechanisms coexist.)
4. **The lesson already existed as history, never as rule.** `CLAUDE.md` §4
   records "cure a CLASSE, não o exemplo (S352)" and §5 records the r22
   lesson ("enumerar não fecha canal instruction-adjacent, remover fecha").
   Neither is process doctrine, which is why the cost kept being paid.

## §3 Decision

Adopt the clause as written in `PROTOCOL.md` §Cure discipline (the signed
text is the source of truth; this ADR records WHY). Operating consequences:

- The round record format gains a `Class:` line per finding. The author of
  the cure writes it; the judgment is explicit, dated and auditable.
- On the second occurrence of a class, the lander treats a record without a
  structural cure or a declared acceptance as a blocking finding against the
  record. This is a process rule today (the lander is a script outside the
  canonical tree); W2 and W3 make it mechanical in their own signatures.
- The rule applies from the first round of the next ceremony onward. It was
  already followed in the S353 night packs before this text landed — the
  plan states that following the rule does not require the canonical text.

## §4 What this amendment does NOT do

- **No reduction of detection.** No round ceiling, no filter, no severity
  that waives review. A refuted hypothesis does not return without new data.
- It does not change the receiving discipline of ADR-140, the VETO model,
  the 3-strike policy, or the verification cascade (V0–V3). A
  `design-coherent` debate outcome still authorizes nothing.
- It does not touch the `receiving-review` skill (SP-NNN governance) — a
  named follow-up: mirror the clause in
  `.claude/skills/core/receiving-review/SKILL.md` through the skill-patch
  route, so the checklist an agent loads carries the cure side too.
- It does not update `PROTOCOL.pt-BR.md` (already out of sync since
  2026-06-11 by its own header; `PROTOCOL.md` wins on divergence).

## §5 Blast radius and Sync Impact Report (PROTOCOL semver: MINOR)

Additive doctrine ⇒ MINOR bump under `docs/PROTOCOL-SEMVER.md`, paired with
this ADR-AMEND. Dependent-set of the Sync Impact Report:

| Dependent artifact | Impact |
|---|---|
| `CLAUDE.md` §Critical Rules | already carries the S352 line «Cure a CLASSE, não o exemplo»; it now points at a PROTOCOL clause instead of standing alone — no edit in this signature |
| `.claude/team.md` / `frontend-team.md` | none (no archetype change) |
| `.claude/skills/core/ceo-orchestration/SKILL.md` | none (no gate change) |
| `PLAN-SCHEMA.md` / `DEBATE-SCHEMA.md` | none; the `Class:` line lives in rail-round records, not in debate critiques |
| `.claude/skills/core/receiving-review/SKILL.md` | follow-up (SP-NNN route), declared in §4 |

## §6 Follow-ups (each its own signature, per Owner decisions 6 and 8)

- **W1** — controls proportional to the risk of the change (PROTOCOL.md).
- **W2** — rail telemetry: one audit event per round that groups a ceremony;
  unknown is ABSENT, never zero (`.claude/hooks/`, SPEC).
- **W3** — safeguard against editing the record: original vs decided
  severity as distinct fields; closure requires zero pending blockers.

## §7 Reversion

Revert path: remove `PROTOCOL.md` §Cure discipline and mark this file
`Status: SUPERSEDED` with a `Superseded-By:` pointer, through a signed
ceremony. No code depends on the clause.
